(*
Fibers — cooperative scheduler. Two fibers each yield twice, appending their tag
to a shared log; run drives them round-robin. Expected interleave: A B A B A B.
R7. Entry declares the `concurrency:` capability.

De-recursify Phase 3 correctness proof (ABBBAA -> ABABAB): this is THE
regression for the old Zephyr-hijack activation-reuse bug. The old recursive
engine + single-shared-C-stack hijack reused one run_interpreter activation
across fibers and produced the WRONG interleave, deterministically
'ABBBAA' (confirmed both on native_sim and via a -D__ZEPHYR__ host repro —
see docs/archive/fiber_implementation.md section 1-2). The flat non-recursive
engine (swap-Stack fiber switch, one mechanism on every target, no
__ZEPHYR__-conditional switch code left in vm.c/gc.c/dispatch.c) must
produce the strictly-alternating 'ABABAB' below. A single accumulated
string makes any deviation from the exact round-robin order (including
'ABBBAA') an immediate, unmissable string mismatch.
expect:
ABABAB
done
skip-oevm: true
*)
class FibersTest usingPlatform: platform concurrency: concurrency = () (
  public main: platform2 args: args = (
    | log |
    log:: ''.                                          (* empty string accumulator *)
    concurrency spawn: [
      log:: log , 'A'. concurrency yield.
      log:: log , 'A'. concurrency yield.
      log:: log , 'A' ].
    concurrency spawn: [
      log:: log , 'B'. concurrency yield.
      log:: log , 'B'. concurrency yield.
      log:: log , 'B' ].
    concurrency run.
    log println.
    'done' println.
    ^ 0
  )
) : (
  public packageUsing: manifest = ( ^ self new )
)
